# Demo and marketing videos, wherever they are saved, and the scripts that cut
# them. Kept out of the repo and off the server (deploy.sh excludes the same
# set) until we decide to host them on the website.
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[mM]4[vV]
*.[wW][eE][bB][mM]
*.[mM][kK][vV]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[wW][mM][vV]
/marketing-video/
/marketing-videos/
# The website's own demo video (docs/ops/website.md) is part of the site.
!/mobile/public/site/video/*.mp4

# Claude Code worktrees — each is a full checkout of this repo. They were
# excluded only in .git/info/exclude, which git honours but EAS CLI does not
# read, so `eas build` descended into every one of them while packing the
# upload. That both bloated the tarball and raced a session removing its own
# worktree (ENOENT on lstat, build aborted). Listing them here is the form
# EAS respects. Not .easignore: that file REPLACES .gitignore for EAS, so a
# minimal one would start shipping node_modules.
.claude/worktrees/
